  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Let's finish.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 980,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 29,
      "word_count": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "With the main idea, for a 90 degree clockwise rotation, a value at row R column C moves to row C column N minus 1 minus R.",
      "start_ms": 1680,
      "end_ms": 14460,
      "start_frame": 50,
      "end_frame": 434,
      "word_count": 27
    },
    {
      "text": "From that one coordinate truth, we found three different solutions.",
      "start_ms": 15180,
      "end_ms": 19800,
      "start_frame": 455,
      "end_frame": 594,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "Method 1, use the destination directly, with an extra matrix.",
      "start_ms": 20560,
      "end_ms": 25300,
      "start_frame": 617,
      "end_frame": 759,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "Method 2, notice that connected destination form four position cycles.",
      "start_ms": 25300,
      "end_ms": 31620,
      "start_frame": 759,
      "end_frame": 949,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "And method 3, split the same mapping into two simpler transformations.",
      "start_ms": 32100,
      "end_ms": 37120,
      "start_frame": 963,
      "end_frame": 1114,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "Transpose, then reverse every row.",
      "start_ms": 37740,
      "end_ms": 41300,
      "start_frame": 1132,
      "end_frame": 1239,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "The most important lesson is bigger than rotate image.",
      "start_ms": 41680,
      "end_ms": 45120,
      "start_frame": 1250,
      "end_frame": 1354,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "When a matrix transformation looks confusing, do not start by memorizing code.",
      "start_ms": 45940,
      "end_ms": 51560,
      "start_frame": 1378,
      "end_frame": 1547,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "First ask, where should one coordinate move?",
      "start_ms": 52120,
      "end_ms": 56200,
      "start_frame": 1564,
      "end_frame": 1686,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "Once you know the coordinate mapping, it may reveal a cycle, a symmetry, or a sequence of simpler transformations.",
      "start_ms": 56940,
      "end_ms": 65340,
      "start_frame": 1708,
      "end_frame": 1960,
      "word_count": 19
    },
    {
      "text": "That way, the code comes from the logic, not from memorization.",
      "start_ms": 66120,
      "end_ms": 71280,
      "start_frame": 1984,
      "end_frame": 2138,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "Question 14, rotate image is complete.",
      "start_ms": 71280,
      "end_ms": 75460,
      "start_frame": 2138,
      "end_frame": 2264,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Our global progress moves from 13 out of 227 to 14 out of 227.",
      "start_ms": 76100,
      "end_ms": 84840,
      "start_frame": 2283,
      "end_frame": 2545,
      "word_count": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "And next, in arrays and hashing.",
      "start_ms": 85300,
      "end_ms": 87780,
      "start_frame": 2559,
      "end_frame": 2633,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Question 15, spiral matrix.",
      "start_ms": 88840,
      "end_ms": 91520,
      "start_frame": 2665,
      "end_frame": 2746,
      "word_count": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "That is up next.",
      "start_ms": 91920,
      "end_ms": 93440,
      "start_frame": 2758,
      "end_frame": 2803,
      "word_count": 4
    }
  ],
